So I've got a knight at the castle. He broke his lance early on and just 
now found a replacement. He also recently got a septum off a troll. So 
the question is, which is really better? The Setpum is two-handed, so no 
shield, and bad news if it get's cursed but isn't too heavy and does 
good damage. The Lance on the is one-handed, and reaches a farther at 
max skill, but weighs over 3 times as much, and really doesn't hit very 
hard.

Or maybe he should forget it and focus on becoming a bad-ass spellcaster 
instead. The lance was certainly handy early on, and worked well with 
the jumping, but maybe he's past the stage where he needs it.

